["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Ducks run on a daily commute: roost, food, rest, food, roost. Be on the route at the right minute.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A mallard&#x27;s day in four panels, 80 percent. Dawn: fly to a cut grain field to feed. Midday: rest on a marsh or raft on open water. Late day: back to the field to feed. Night: marsh or creek to roost. Legal hours for ducks: 30 minutes before sunrise to 30 minutes after sunset, 99 percent. Wigeon raft offshore until late afternoon. After a cold front with a north wind, hunt the next morning, 65 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A mallard&#x27;s day (80%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"6\" y=\"40\" width=\"92\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6d7b0\"/>\n  <text x=\"52\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dawn</text>\n  <rect x=\"14\" y=\"130\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/>\n  <path d=\"M18 130 v-8 M30 130 v-8 M42 130 v-8 M54 130 v-8 M66 130 v-8 M78 130 v-8\" stroke=\"#a88f3d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(52 98) scale(0.7)\"><ellipse rx=\"18\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-1\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M8 -3 Q2 -20.0 -10 -32.0 Q-8 -16.0 -8 -3Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M8 3 Q2 20.0 -10 32.0 Q-8 16.0 -8 3Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-16 0 L-26 -5 L-26 5Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"52\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fly to cut</text>\n  <text x=\"52\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">grain field</text>\n  <rect x=\"104\" y=\"40\" width=\"92\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\"/>\n  <text x=\"150\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Midday</text>\n  <rect x=\"112\" y=\"134\" width=\"76\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(144 132) scale(0.6)\"><path d=\"M-30 0 Q-34 -14 -18 -14 L10 -12 Q24 -10 24 0 Q20 10 -2 10 L-22 10 Q-32 8 -30 0Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-20\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M26 -21 L38 -18 L26 -15Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M180 134 v-30 M184 134 v-24\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"150\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rest on marsh</text>\n  <text x=\"150\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">or raft</text>\n  <rect x=\"202\" y=\"40\" width=\"92\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6d7b0\"/>\n  <text x=\"248\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Late day</text>\n  <rect x=\"210\" y=\"130\" width=\"76\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/>\n  <path d=\"M214 130 v-8 M226 130 v-8 M238 130 v-8 M250 130 v-8 M262 130 v-8 M274 130 v-8\" stroke=\"#a88f3d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(248 98) scale(0.7)\"><ellipse rx=\"18\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-1\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M8 -3 Q2 -20.0 -10 -32.0 Q-8 -16.0 -8 -3Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M8 3 Q2 20.0 -10 32.0 Q-8 16.0 -8 3Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-16 0 L-26 -5 L-26 5Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"248\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Back to field</text>\n  <text x=\"248\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">to feed</text>\n  <rect x=\"300\" y=\"40\" width=\"92\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#b9c2cf\"/>\n  <text x=\"346\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Night</text>\n  <rect x=\"308\" y=\"134\" width=\"76\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(340 132) scale(0.6)\"><path d=\"M-30 0 Q-34 -14 -18 -14 L10 -12 Q24 -10 24 0 Q20 10 -2 10 L-22 10 Q-32 8 -30 0Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-20\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M26 -21 L38 -18 L26 -15Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M376 134 v-30 M380 134 v-24\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"346\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Marsh, creek</text>\n  <text x=\"346\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">to roost</text>\n  <rect x=\"6\" y=\"214\" width=\"388\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Legal: 30 min before sunrise to 30 min after sunset</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wigeon raft offshore until late afternoon (80%)</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cold front, north wind: hunt the next morning (65%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Fields at dawn and late day. Water at midday and night <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Legal from 30 minutes before sunrise <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the daily pattern</summary><ul><li>Mallards feed early morning and late afternoon in harvested fields, then return to marshes and creeks for the night <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Wigeon raft offshore until late afternoon, then move into marshes and ponds to feed <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Redheads spend the day rafted on deep water and feed morning and evening in the shallows <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Legal hours: half an hour before sunrise to half an hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds/17\">Rule Book</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A 24 hour clock of a mallard&#x27;s day, 80 percent, midnight at the top. Night: roost. Dawn: a flight out to feed. Morning: feed in fields or shallows. Midday: rest on open water. Late afternoon: feed again. Dusk: a flight back to roost. An outer green ring marks legal hours, from half an hour before sunrise to half an hour after sunset. Hunting pressure moves feeding into the night, 75 percent.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A mallard&#x27;s day clock (80%)</text><path d=\"M30.8 154.5 A88 88 0 0 1 206.0 166.0 L158.0 166.0 A40 40 0 0 0 78.3 160.8 Z\" fill=\"#3d4a63\"/><path d=\"M206.0 166.0 A88 88 0 0 1 199.3 199.7 L155.0 181.3 A40 40 0 0 0 158.0 166.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M199.3 199.7 A88 88 0 0 1 151.7 247.3 L133.3 203.0 A40 40 0 0 0 155.0 181.3 Z\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/><path d=\"M151.7 247.3 A88 88 0 0 1 48.2 219.6 L86.3 190.4 A40 40 0 0 0 133.3 203.0 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><path d=\"M48.2 219.6 A88 88 0 0 1 30.8 177.5 L78.3 171.2 A40 40 0 0 0 86.3 190.4 Z\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/><path d=\"M30.8 177.5 A88 88 0 0 1 30.8 154.5 L78.3 160.8 A40 40 0 0 0 78.3 171.2 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M215.2 153.2 A98 98 0 1 1 20.8 153.2 L28.8 154.3 A90 90 0 1 0 207.2 154.3 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"118\" cy=\"166\" r=\"38\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"118\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">24 h</text><text x=\"118.0\" y=\"67.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">0</text><text x=\"222.0\" y=\"171.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"118.00000000000001\" y=\"275.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">12</text><text x=\"14.0\" y=\"171.00000000000003\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">18</text><rect x=\"236\" y=\"70\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#3d4a63\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Night:</text><text x=\"262\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">roost</text><rect x=\"236\" y=\"104\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Flights:</text><text x=\"262\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">dawn and dusk</text><rect x=\"236\" y=\"138\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Feed:</text><text x=\"262\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">fields, shallows</text><rect x=\"236\" y=\"172\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Midday:</text><text x=\"262\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">rest on water</text><rect x=\"236\" y=\"206\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"221\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Outer ring:</text><text x=\"262\" y=\"237\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">legal hours</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pressure moves feeding into the night (75%)</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Two flights a day: out to feed, back to rest <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>The first 30 minutes of legal light are prime (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how the clock shifts</summary><ul><li>GPS (Global Positioning System) tracked mallards under pressure made about two flights a day <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>The clock moves with sunrise. In October sunrise gets later each week, so the dawn flight does too (Tip).</li><li>Where hunting is heavy, the feeding flight shifts to after dark and the birds are back on the refuge before dawn <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Old hand's rule (opinion, widely taught): \"Be set up and quiet before the first bird can see.\"</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Table of weather and ducks with the evidence level. Freeze up and snow cover push ducks south: strong, 80 percent. Hunting pressure sends them to refuges by day: strong, 80 percent. Wind: they land into it, strong, 80 percent. Moonlit windy nights: they leave to feed earlier, medium, 75 percent. A cold front with a north wind brings new birds the next day: hunter lore, 65 percent. Rain and low cloud: they fly lower and later, a tip. The barometer alone: no good study found, verify.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Weather and ducks: how sure are we?</text><rect x=\"4\" y=\"36\" width=\"392\" height=\"33\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Freeze up, snow</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Pushes them south</text><rect x=\"306\" y=\"40\" width=\"86\" height=\"25\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Strong 80%</text><rect x=\"4\" y=\"73\" width=\"392\" height=\"33\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#eef2e6\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunting pressure</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Refuge by day</text><rect x=\"306\" y=\"77\" width=\"86\" height=\"25\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Strong 80%</text><rect x=\"4\" y=\"110\" width=\"392\" height=\"33\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wind</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Land into it</text><rect x=\"306\" y=\"114\" width=\"86\" height=\"25\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Strong 80%</text><rect x=\"4\" y=\"147\" width=\"392\" height=\"33\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#eef2e6\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Moonlit windy night</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Leave to feed early</text><rect x=\"306\" y=\"151\" width=\"86\" height=\"25\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#d9a23a\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Medium 75%</text><rect x=\"4\" y=\"184\" width=\"392\" height=\"33\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cold front, N wind</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">New birds next day</text><rect x=\"306\" y=\"188\" width=\"86\" height=\"25\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#d9a23a\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lore 65%</text><rect x=\"4\" y=\"221\" width=\"392\" height=\"33\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#eef2e6\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Rain, low cloud</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Fly lower, later</text><rect x=\"306\" y=\"225\" width=\"86\" height=\"25\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#b9c2cf\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tip</text><rect x=\"4\" y=\"258\" width=\"392\" height=\"33\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Barometer alone</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">No good study</text><rect x=\"306\" y=\"262\" width=\"86\" height=\"25\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#b9c2cf\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">VERIFY</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Ice, snow and pressure: strong evidence <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Barometer on its own: no good study found (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the evidence behind each line</summary><ul><li>Freeze up and snow: a Missouri study built a weather severity index from cold, days below freezing and snow cover. When it passed a threshold, mallards were more likely to leave <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Warmer winters with less snow are expected to delay fall migration, most for mallards and least for pintails <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Wind: ducks land into the wind <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Moon: waterfowl leave to feed earlier on moonlit, windy nights than on dark, calm nights <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Full moon makes mornings slow because ducks fed all night: hunter lore, not shown in a study found here (Tip).</li><li>Cold front with a north wind brings new birds: hunter lore, widely repeated <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Barometric pressure on its own: no duck study found. Pressure falls before a front, so it may only be a sign of the front (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, a map with north at the top. A blue cold front line moves south. Behind it, on a north wind, a flock of new ducks flies south and drops onto your pond. End card: hunt the morning after the front passes, 65 percent, hunter lore.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A cold front pushes new ducks in</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"34\" width=\"380\" height=\"214\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">N</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"30.0\" y2=\"68.0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"30.0,62.0 24.0,73.0 36.0,73.0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"250\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Your pond</text><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" from=\"0 40\" to=\"0 150\" dur=\"6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><path d=\"M20 0 L380 0\" stroke=\"#3a6fb0\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><polygon points=\"30,0 40,0 35,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><polygon points=\"64,0 74,0 69,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><polygon points=\"98,0 108,0 103,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><polygon points=\"132,0 142,0 137,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><polygon points=\"166,0 176,0 171,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><polygon points=\"200,0 210,0 205,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><polygon points=\"234,0 244,0 239,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><polygon points=\"268,0 278,0 273,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><polygon points=\"302,0 312,0 307,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><polygon points=\"336,0 346,0 341,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/><polygon points=\"370,0 380,0 375,12\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\"/></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"200 40;200 40;160 188\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;1\" dur=\"6.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><ellipse rx=\"3\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"10;3;10\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"16\"/></ellipse></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"226 50;226 50;194 198\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;1\" dur=\"6.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><ellipse rx=\"3\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"10;3;10\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"16\"/></ellipse></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"252 36;252 36;228 184\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;1\" dur=\"6.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><ellipse rx=\"3\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"10;3;10\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"16\"/></ellipse></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"278 48;278 48;262 196\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;1\" dur=\"6.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><ellipse rx=\"3\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"10;3;10\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"16\"/></ellipse></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"304 40;304 40;296 188\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;1\" dur=\"6.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><ellipse rx=\"3\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"10;3;10\" dur=\".4s\" repeatCount=\"16\"/></ellipse></g><text x=\"330\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#3a6fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">North wind</text><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.6s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"256\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunt the morning after it passes (65%, lore)</text></g></svg>\n<figcaption>A cold front pushes new ducks in. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Hunt the morning after a front passes (65%, lore).</li><li>New birds decoy better than the locals (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: reading a front</summary><ul><li>A <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Cold front\">Cold front</button> brings a wind shift to the north or northwest, colder air and often clearer skies (Tip).</li><li>Migrating ducks ride tailwinds. A tracked mallard was clocked at about 165 km/h (103 mph) ground speed on a strong tailwind <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Before the front: birds may feed hard (Tip). After it: fresh birds on new water <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Check forecasts 3 days ahead and plan your ponds for the morning after (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view of a J hook spread with the wind blowing left to right. Three ducks fly in from downwind, pass high over the spread, circle back, then turn and glide in against the wind, wings cupped, landing in the open pocket in front of the hide.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#cfe0ea\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"240\" width=\"400\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"236\" width=\"70\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"185\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text><path d=\"M20 22 L110 22\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><polygon points=\"106,13 106,31 124,22\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"132\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">WIND</text><g transform=\"translate(70 200) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(55 180) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(52 158) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(62 138) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(84 128) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(100 208) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(118 214) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(78 214) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(110 120) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(140 110) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(172 104) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(205 100) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(238 98) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(270 98) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(302 100) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(334 104) scale(1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-8\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"168\" rx=\"58\" ry=\"32\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" opacity=\".5\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\"/><path d=\"M400 60 C 300 40, 160 40, 90 70 C 30 100, 60 150, 150 150 C 250 150, 360 160, 380 168 C 330 168, 280 168, 205 168\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 6\" opacity=\".5\"/><g><animateMotion dur=\"6.5s\" begin=\"0s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;1\" keyTimes=\"0;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M400 60 C 300 40, 160 40, 90 70 C 30 100, 60 150, 150 150 C 250 150, 360 160, 380 168 C 330 168, 280 168, 205 168\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 -14)\"><g transform=\"scale(1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;4;14\" dur=\".5s\" repeatCount=\"12\"/><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;5\" begin=\"5.6s\" dur=\".6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g></g></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"6.5s\" begin=\"0.25s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;1\" keyTimes=\"0;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M400 60 C 300 40, 160 40, 90 70 C 30 100, 60 150, 150 150 C 250 150, 360 160, 380 168 C 330 168, 280 168, 205 168\"/><g transform=\"translate(-6 0)\"><g transform=\"scale(1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;4;14\" dur=\".5s\" repeatCount=\"12\"/><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;5\" begin=\"5.6s\" dur=\".6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g></g></g><g><animateMotion dur=\"6.5s\" begin=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;1\" keyTimes=\"0;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M400 60 C 300 40, 160 40, 90 70 C 30 100, 60 150, 150 150 C 250 150, 360 160, 380 168 C 330 168, 280 168, 205 168\"/><g transform=\"translate(-12 14)\"><g transform=\"scale(1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\"><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;4;14\" dur=\".5s\" repeatCount=\"12\"/><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"14;5\" begin=\"5.6s\" dur=\".6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g></g></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0\" begin=\"4.2s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"388\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">They circle, look</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.8s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"232\" y=\"196\" width=\"160\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Land INTO the wind</text></g></svg>\n<figcaption>Ducks circle, then land into the wind. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Wind sets the landing direction <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Windy days push ducks to calm, sheltered water (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: wind and rain in practice</summary><ul><li>Ducks land into the wind; set the spread so they cross in front of you (80% landing, Tip setup).</li><li>Strong wind: ducks hold on the lee side of ponds and sloughs <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Rain and low cloud: ducks often fly lower and move later in the morning (Tip).</li><li>Calm, clear \"bluebird\" days: ducks fly high and decoy poorly (Tip, widely reported).</li><li>Cold rain plus wind is the hardest on you: plan for cold water safety. See <a href=\"#/s/first-duck-hunt/10\">Boat and kayak safety</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Moon</th><th>What ducks do</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bright, windy night</td><td>Leave to feed earlier</td><td>Medium <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Full moon</td><td>Feed all night, slow morning</td><td>Lore (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Dark, calm night</td><td>Leave later</td><td>Medium <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>The moon is a small factor. Pressure and weather are bigger (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what the research says</summary><ul><li>Ducks Unlimited (Ducks after dark): waterfowl leave to feed earlier on moonlit, windy nights than dark, calm nights <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Full moon claims for duck hunting are mostly field stories, not studies (70% that no study backs them).</li><li>A deer study found little moon effect on buck movement, a reminder not to over trust the moon <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map sketch. A refuge lake with no hunting on the left, a grain field or marsh on the right. Ducks fly from the refuge to the food at dusk and back before dawn. GPS tracked mallards made about 2 flights a day and avoided heavily hunted areas during shooting hours, 80 percent. Hunt the line between safety and food, a tip.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunted ducks: safe by day, food by night</text><ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"130\" rx=\"74\" ry=\"50\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">No hunting</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">refuge</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"70\" width=\"140\" height=\"110\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grain field</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">or marsh</text><path d=\"M160 104 Q205 70 248 96\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"92\" x2=\"244.85504244572473\" y2=\"94.91302546743484\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"250.0,98.0 243.7,87.2 237.5,97.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M248 156 Q205 186 160 158\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><line x1=\"168\" y1=\"162\" x2=\"163.14495755427527\" y2=\"159.08697453256516\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"158.0,156.0 164.3,166.8 170.5,156.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"205\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dusk</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Before dawn</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"212\" width=\"380\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">GPS mallards: about 2 flights a day,</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">hide from heavy hunting in shooting hours (80%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunt the line between safe and food (Tip)</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Pressure moves feeding into the dark <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Weekdays and quiet spots beat Saturday crowds (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pressure facts</summary><ul><li>West Tennessee: the study area was hunted almost every day; mallards avoided hunted ground during shooting hours <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Disturbing their refuges cut the landscape's daily shotgun volleys by about a third: ducks hunkered down and moved less <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Mallards prioritize safety, then food, and keep commutes short <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: find where the refuge birds feed and the line they fly. Hunt that line at first and last light (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-redhead-flight.jpg\" alt=\"Redheads raft by day and feed at the ends of the day.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Redheads raft by day and feed at the ends of the day. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Redheads_Lake_Andes_National_Wildlife_Refuge_South_Dakota_(53921083806).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Puddle ducks: dawn and dusk to fields and shallows <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Divers raft by day, feed in the shallows early and late <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: by species</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Duck</th><th>Daily habit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mallard</td><td>Fields at dawn and late day; marsh at night <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Wigeon</td><td>Raft offshore until late afternoon <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Redhead</td><td>Raft on deep water by day; feed morning and evening <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Bufflehead, scaup, ring necked</td><td>Feed more by day than at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Mergansers</td><td>Feed almost only in daylight <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Gadwall (studied in Louisiana)</td><td>Feed and rest more at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Diving ducks on the Great Lakes leave roosts at dusk and feed overnight near shore <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>\"Fields at dawn, water at noon\"</td><td>Mallard day <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>2 flights</td><td>Refuge to food and back <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"North wind, new birds\"</td><td>Cold front (65%, lore)</td></tr><tr><td>\"Ice and snow push; the barometer only whispers\"</td><td>Evidence levels</td></tr><tr><td>\"Bright windy night, early flight\"</td><td>Moon <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Old hand's rule (opinion, widely taught): \"Be in the blind before the birds can see you, and stay till the last legal minute.\"</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li>\"Bluebird day, ducks stay away.\" Calm, clear days are slow (Tip).</li><li>\"Pressure pushes ducks into the dark.\" <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Main source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily pattern</td><td>Ducks Unlimited ID guides</td></tr><tr><td>Night, moon</td><td>Ducks Unlimited, Ducks after dark</td></tr><tr><td>Weather</td><td>Schummer and others, 2010</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source, with date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.ca/assets/2021/10/waterfowl-ID-guide-2020-EN-reader-spreads.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited Canada ID guide</a>: daily habits of mallard, wigeon, redhead. Checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://ducks.org/conservation/waterfowl-research-science/ducks-after-dark\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, Ducks after dark (Dale Humburg, 2009)</a>: night migration, night feeding by species, moon and wind, pressure. Read directly 2026-10-11 (70 to 80%).</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/conservation/waterfowl-research-science/understanding-waterfowl-the-science-of-disturbance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, Understanding waterfowl: the science of disturbance (2026)</a>. Read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://bioone.org/journals/Journal-of-Wildlife-Management/volume-74/issue-1/2008-524/Weather-Related-Indices-of-AutumnWinter-Dabbling-Duck-Abundance-in-Middle/10.2193/2008-524.full\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Schummer and others, Journal of Wildlife Management (2010)</a> and <a href=\"https://doaj.org/article/fcecb1b945284c65a02c757f117ac2dd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Notaro and others, PLoS ONE (2016)</a>: weather severity index, delayed migration. Search preview 2026-10-11 (70 to 80%).</li><li><a href=\"https://www.outdoorlife.com/hunting/duck-flies-record-speed\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Life, mallard clocked at 103 mph</a>: GPS ground speed on a tailwind. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://outdoorlife.com/articles/hunting/2015/10/three-tips-hunting-wood-ducks-creeks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Life, creek tips</a> and <a href=\"https://www.grandviewoutdoors.com/bird-hunting/waterfowl/jump-shooting-revised\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grand View Outdoors, jump shooting revised</a>: ducks hold on the lee side. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://myfwc.com/hunting/waterfowl/hunt-guide/hunt-tips/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Florida Fish and Wildlife Conservation Commission, waterfowl hunt tips</a>: landing into wind. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://fieldandstream.com/stories/hunting/deer-hunting/whitetail-hunting/moon-phase-deer-hunting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Field and Stream, moon phase and deer</a>: little moon effect on bucks. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Legal hours: app Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>"]